{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540623-aquatic-mages","id":1540623,"title":"Aquatic Mages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-18T07:32:23-07:00","id":1540623,"title":"Aquatic Mages?","content":"<br /> I'm trying to complete the old <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a> document by adding at least one NPC for every official supernatural template, but I'm having difficulty finding full stats for aquatic or nautical-oriented mages, especially ones from 1e. Do you know of any sea hags, weather wizards, or marine magicians that would make suitable antagonists for a maritime chronicle? If so, please post them here and I'll add them to the doc (which I plan on asking Mr Gone to store on his website as a backup, so the wiki isn't lost forever if my Google Docs account ever goes down).<br /> <br /> If there aren't any suitable pregen characters, I was thinking of rolling up one of my own. Maybe a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_gale\" target=\"_blank\">witch of November</a> or an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Man_of_the_Sea\" target=\"_blank\">Old Man of the Sea</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T07:43:13-07:00","id":1540624,"title":"","content":"Given that mages are addicted to Mystery, maybe a Jacques Cousteau character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</spa